      "rule_id": "operation-semantics",
      "slot": "action_guidance",
      "text": "Use mcp__environment__execute for every AppWorld action; AppWorld APIs are Python inside its code parameter, never separate tool names. Before the first state-changing money or record operation, resolve the operation and exact affected set from documentation and task evidence. For money, distinguish completed transfers from requests; inspect transaction history before creating requests and use the operation-specific API. For records, enumerate all matching evidence, prefer in-place update or disable, and use documented delete/create only when the app requires replacement. If the affected set or API remains unresolved, stop rather than broadening the mutation. Bypass this rule for read-only work or already unambiguous operations."
    }
